{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RCA (rebar-debug Phase 1, root cause PROVEN + runtime-confirmed):\n\nMECHANISM: story-1734 multi-project fan-out in fetcher._build_snapshot builds one inbound query per key in .bridge_state/projects.json: project_list = list(read_projects().keys()) or [_query_project]. The live tickets branch's projects.json was overwritten with the rehearsal fixture {LEG,ONE,TWO,ZERO / legacy_default:null}; LEG/ONE/TWO/ZERO do not exist in live REB Jira. So the first query jql_active('LEG') = 'project = LEG AND status != \"Done\"' is rejected by Jira (value leg does not exist for field project) -> ACLI exit 1 -> reconcile_once raises -> pass exits 1.\n\nRUNTIME PROOF: (1) CI log run 31887498540 shows the exact failing ACLI command 'project = LEG AND status != \"Done\"'. (2) Local repro: jqls_for('LEG')[0] == 'project = LEG AND status != \"Done\"' (byte-identical). (3) _PROJECT_KEY_RE accepts 'LEG' (syntactically valid) so no validator catches a nonexistent-but-well-formed key.\n\nDISCRIMINATING EVIDENCE (rules out alternatives): first-failure bisect on Reconcile Bridge runs isolates the consistent-failure onset at 2026-08-15T02:39Z; git log of origin/tickets:.bridge_state/projects.json shows commit 9f1b2cff98 ('commit mapping') + 275bd7507e ('scrub'), authored 't <t@t.co>' (the test-fixture git identity), at 2026-08-14T19:18-0700 (=08-15T02:18Z) — 21 min before onset. Not a code regression: the fan-out code is unchanged and correct; the DATA is wrong. The corruption arrived via AD-HOC git commits on the live tickets branch (the exact practice AGENTS.md bans), not via the isolated DC rehearsal harness (which uses random scratch keys + REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=off).\n\nLEGITIMACY: defect (production breakage). Authoritative intended state = the ensure-registry seed {version:1, legacy_default:'REB', projects:{}} (project_ensures.seed_projects_mapping_unit), which is also the green-run state (commit 0d9f4b8459). Fix = restore that canonical mapping on origin/tickets."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786805227115944001,"uuid":"6f9e715e-adda-43e0-bbad-b0abbadadca4"}